    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nOn macOS, if `$LANG` has no codeset, `LANG=en_GB` for example, yanking to `\"+` stores\r\n\"M√ºller\" instead of \"Müller\".  pbcopy/pbpaste take their encoding from the\r\nlocale env vars and fall back to MacRoman:\r\n\r\n    printf 'Müller' | LANG=en_GB pbcopy; pbpaste    # M√ºller\r\n\r\nThe same happens after `:language en_GB` or with a non-UTF-8 `$LC_ALL`.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nRun pbcopy/pbpaste with `LC_CTYPE=UTF-8` and `LC_ALL` unset. Nvim text is always \r\nUTF-8. Nvim's own environment and other child processes are unchanged.\r\n\r\nFixes #11432 (the pbcopy/pbpaste part)\r\nAI-assisted.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-01T10:21:48Z",
